[AMAZON_PRODUCTS MARKET INTEL]
Amazon's 2025 bestsellers reveal a consumer stratified into two tribes: COMFORT MAXIMIZERS (bulk essentials, wireless comfort apparel, meal prep tools) optimizing for convenience and value; and IDENTITY ARCHITECTS (Stanley/Owala drinkers, K-beauty skincare users, colorway-conscious buyers) purchasing premium-feeling products to signal health consciousness, taste, and lifestyle values. The middle tier is collapsing—brands are winning either via trust-through-ubiquity (Amazon Basics, Charmin, Hanes) or via aspirational identity positioning (Stanley's $35+ price premium justified by social status). Skincare and drinkware are the battlegrounds because they offer daily identity expression. The biggest blind spot: pricing transparency is GONE from bestseller listings, indicating Amazon's confidence in algorithmic lock-in—buyers trust the platform more than the price. Opportunity: vertical integration across identity categories (water bottle → skincare → apparel matching aesthetic identity) and subscription models (recurring purchase optimization).

